{"When an ASN.1 element is encoded with indefinite length (length byte 0x80), readLength() returns -1, but callers like readInteger() pass this directly to read(int length), which will try to allocate a byte array with negative size and throw a NegativeArraySizeException instead of a controlled IOException": 0.8942590951919556, "Introducing a new abstract method order() in a widely implemented SPI interface will break binary compatibility and can cause AbstractMethodError at runtime for existing CryptoProvider implementations compiled against older versions - should provide a default implementation": 0.9291154742240906, "The service provider configuration only registers the new crypto provider and omits the default one; if existing code or tests rely on the default CryptoProvider still being available on the classpath, they will no longer be able to load it via ServiceLoader": 0.19605004787445068}